<!--Render Target Documentation — PropertyRenderer
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.PropertyRenderer-->
<rdoc:PropertyRenderer xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    MBOM properties to settings entries
  </is>
  <documentation>
    The property renderer fills a SettingsBundle. V1 emission is a pseudo-map
    pair ["paramName", value] per entry.

    Native parameter inventory and scad:value defaults come from NativeBlock.bml
    in @machineblocks/core. There is no hardcoded parameter list in this
    package. The old 09_mbom_properties.yml file is a pointer stub only.

    Each property definition supplies:

    - name — MBOM property name, camelCase
    - scadName — SCAD parameter name, camelCase, usually identical
    - type — MBOM type FQN
    - serializer — rule from SerializationRules
    - default — default value

    V1 reads property values from memberValues and definition defaults, not via
    accessor capabilities.

    Native properties (those declared on the NativeBlock set) map to dedicated
    getters in the generated module body:

        size      = mb_param_size(config, settings, [1, 8, 9]);
        baseColor = mb_param_baseColor(config, settings);

    Custom properties map to the generic getter:

        wallThickness  = mb_param(config, settings, "wallThickness", 1);
        cornerRounding = mb_param(config, settings, "cornerRounding", 0.5);

    Native versus custom is decided from the domain TypeRegistry (the
    NativeBlock property set), not from a list in this package.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:ExpressionRenderer" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:PropertyRenderer>
